    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "s = \"ABAB\", k = 2       ->  4   (replace both A's, or both B's)\ns = \"AABABBA\", k = 1    ->  4   (\"AABA\" -> \"AAAA\")\ns = \"AABBBCC\", k = 0    ->  3   (\"BBB\", no changes allowed)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: replace everything but the most common letter"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Look at any window. The cheapest way to make it all one letter is to keep its **most common** letter and replace the rest. So a window works exactly when `length - (count of its most common letter) <= k`."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "That condition behaves well as the window moves: growing the window can only make it harder to satisfy, and shrinking it from the left makes it easier. That's the shape a **variable-size sliding window** needs. Grow the right edge one letter at a time; whenever the window needs more than k replacements, shrink the left edge until it doesn't; and remember the longest window seen."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: every start, growing right"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function characterReplacement(s, k) {\n  let best = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n    const count = new Array(26).fill(0);\n    let maxFreq = 0;\n    for (let j = i; j < s.length; j++) {\n      const c = s.charCodeAt(j) - 65;\n      maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, ++count[c]);\n      if (j - i + 1 - maxFreq <= k) best = Math.max(best, j - i + 1);   // s[i..j] works\n    }\n  }\n  return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def character_replacement(s, k):\n    best = 0\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        count = [0] * 26\n        max_freq = 0\n        for j in range(i, len(s)):\n            c = ord(s[j]) - ord(\"A\")\n            count[c] += 1\n            max_freq = max(max_freq, count[c])\n            if j - i + 1 - max_freq <= k:\n                best = max(best, j - i + 1)   # s[i..j] works\n    return best"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int characterReplacement(String s, int k) {\n    int best = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n        int[] count = new int[26];\n        int maxFreq = 0;\n        for (int j = i; j < s.length(); j++) {\n            maxFreq = Math.max(maxFreq, ++count[s.charAt(j) - 'A']);\n            if (j - i + 1 - maxFreq <= k) best = Math.max(best, j - i + 1);   // s[i..j] works\n        }\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int characterReplacement(string s, int k) {\n    int best = 0, n = s.size();\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int count[26] = {0};\n        int maxFreq = 0;\n        for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {\n            maxFreq = max(maxFreq, ++count[s[j] - 'A']);\n            if (j - i + 1 - maxFreq <= k) best = max(best, j - i + 1);   // s[i..j] works\n        }\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(1).** Every pair (start, end) is looked at once."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Sliding window"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "character-replacement",
      "caption": "The window grows right; when it needs more than k replacements, it shrinks from the left. Try k = 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function characterReplacement(s, k) {\n  const count = new Array(26).fill(0);\n  let left = 0, best = 0;\n  for (let right = 0; right < s.length; right++) {\n    count[s.charCodeAt(right) - 65]++;               // 'A' is 65\n    // To make the window one letter, replace everything except its most common letter.\n    while (right - left + 1 - Math.max(...count) > k) {\n      count[s.charCodeAt(left) - 65]--;              // too many to replace: shrink from the left\n      left++;\n    }\n    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);\n  }\n  return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def character_replacement(s, k):\n    count = [0] * 26\n    left = best = 0\n    for right in range(len(s)):\n        count[ord(s[right]) - ord(\"A\")] += 1\n        # To make the window one letter, replace everything except its most common letter.\n        while right - left + 1 - max(count) > k:\n            count[ord(s[left]) - ord(\"A\")] -= 1      # too many to replace: shrink from the left\n            left += 1\n        best = max(best, right - left + 1)\n    return best"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int characterReplacement(String s, int k) {\n    int[] count = new int[26];\n    int left = 0, best = 0;\n    for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {\n        count[s.charAt(right) - 'A']++;\n        // To make the window one letter, replace everything except its most common letter.\n        while (right - left + 1 - Arrays.stream(count).max().getAsInt() > k) {\n            count[s.charAt(left) - 'A']--;       // too many to replace: shrink from the left\n            left++;\n        }\n        best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int characterReplacement(string s, int k) {\n    int count[26] = {0};\n    int left = 0, best = 0;\n    for (int right = 0; right < (int)s.size(); right++) {\n        count[s[right] - 'A']++;\n        // To make the window one letter, replace everything except its most common letter.\n        while (right - left + 1 - *max_element(count, count + 26) > k) {\n            count[s[left] - 'A']--;              // too many to replace: shrink from the left\n            left++;\n        }\n        best = max(best, right - left + 1);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(1).** `left` and `right` each move at most n times; finding the largest of 26 counts is a constant amount of work per step."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A famous refinement keeps `maxFreq` as a running maximum that **never goes down**, and shrinks with `if` instead of `while`. It looks wrong — the window's real maximum can drop — but the answer only improves when a window beats the best so far, and that needs a genuinely higher `maxFreq`. It saves the 26-count scan; mention it if asked."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Brute force: every start, growing right",
          "time": "O(n²)",
          "timeWhy": "Every **(start, end)** pair is looked at once.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "**26 counters**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Sliding window",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "`left` and `right` each move **at most n** times.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "**26 counters** and the best count."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**k = 0** — the longest run of one letter.",
        "**k at least the length** — the whole string works.",
        "**All the same letter** — the whole string, with no replacements.",
        "**The best letter changes along the string** — the window keeps counts of every letter, so it doesn't matter which one ends up most common."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Max Consecutive Ones III** — the same window on a binary array: at most k zeros may be flipped.",
        "**Longest Substring with At Most K Distinct Characters** — shrink when the window has more than k different letters (Hash Map course).",
        "**Minimum Window Substring** — the variable window turned around: shrink while the window is still valid, to find the *shortest*. Next lesson."
      ]
    }
  ],
